"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative introduced by Alex, with Sarah Tan as the lead and a $500,000 budget for phase one. The project has seen several developments: five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture joined the team in September; the design phase was completed, leading to the development phase led by Omar Jensen; a significant milestone was reached with the successful completion of the testing phase, celebrated in October; and phase two has achieved a breakthrough in predictive analytics, with a detailed report to be shared in November. Additionally, the team is seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype by the end of November, and security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption, effective January next year. A training budget of $15,000 has also been approved for the coding team and project managers."
